tests/atf/run-atf.sh                : manual : AtfTcpSocket PRODUCES NOTHING. It has the serial log every other harness has (aa658929) and prints not one byte on it -- not the first statement of atfc_run(), not a pre-main constructor -- so there is no DH0:.done and the run ends at the timeout. NOT the guest stack: unchanged under `stack 200000`. NOT the missing mathieeedoubbas.library: staged, and the behaviour is unchanged. A pre-push tree took `Exception 3 ... at ffffffff` at 12.8 s; the landed binary takes no exception at all and hangs silently, and the only difference is one dropped serial call, i.e. code layout. A fault that moves with layout is memory corruption, not a fixed bad jump, so where it dies is not yet established. Do not wire it until it runs
tests/tools/run-livetools.sh       : manual : SLIRP. the regression test for "the command says the network is down while it is up" (v0.2.0 shipped ping, netstat and ShowNetStatus with their live paths dead). The guest's command list is written before the boot and embeds SLIRP's gateway in five commands -- `ping 10.0.2.2`, and the three AddNetRoute/DeleteNetRoute lines that add, clear and restore the default route -- and two assertions compare against the literals 10.0.2.15 and 10.0.2.2. To run bridged it needs the segment's gateway discovered on the host (`ip route show default dev <iface>`) and substituted into both, and the leased-address assertion read out of the transcript rather than compared to a constant
